-Beach_at_Charmouth_%2831833309203%29.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Beach_at_Charmouth_%2831833309203%29.jpg/500px-Beach_at_Charmouth_%2831833309203%29.jpg","caption":"Charmouth Beach","author":"Tanya Hart","licence":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Beach_at_Charmouth_(31833309203).jpg","w":5540,"h":3786,"ok_print":true},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Shoreline_on_The_Fleet_-_geograph.org.uk_-_2771449.jpg/960px-Shoreline_on_The_Fleet_-_geograph.org.uk_-_2771449.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Shoreline_on_The_Fleet_-_geograph.org.uk_-_2771449.jpg/500px-Shoreline_on_The_Fleet_-_geograph.org.uk_-_2771449.jpg","caption":"The Fleet","author":"Colin Smith","licence":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shoreline_on_The_Fleet_-_geograph.org.uk_-_2771449.jpg","w":4288,"h":3216,"ok_print":true}],"intro":{"lead":"Fossil cliffs, Durdle Door's stone arch and 185 million years of coastline in Dorset","short":"The Jurassic Coast is a protected shoreline in the United Kingdom, listed by UNESCO. Lyme Regis Museum, Shute Barton and Musbury Castle break up the walk, and Monmouth Beach and Charmouth Beach lie alongside. Its sights run to seven hours, best June to August.","short_src":"rewrite","facts":{"population":4712,"visit_h":5.1}},"do":[{"name":"Durdle Door","type":"activity","detail":"The limestone arch standing out in the sea, and the picture the whole coast is known by. Five minutes on foot from the car park, then steps down to the beach.","evidence":{"n_sources":9,"of":14,"urls":["https://www.visit-dorset.com/blog/post/top-10-things-to-do-on-the-jurassic-coast-in-dorset/","https://anywhereweroam.com/dorset-jurassic-coast/","https://www.helenonherholidays.com/jurassic-coast-11-things-to-do/"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Lulworth Cove","type":"activity","detail":"An almost perfect circle of water with a narrow mouth, cut where the sea broke through one hard band of rock into softer stuff behind. Visitor centre in the village, and the walk to Durdle Door starts here.","evidence":{"n_sources":8,"of":14,"urls":["https://www.visit-dorset.com/blog/post/top-10-things-to-do-on-the-jurassic-coast-in-dorset/","https://anywhereweroam.com/dorset-jurassic-coast/","https://dorsettravelguide.com/dorset-jurassic-coast-highlights/"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Fossil hunting at Lyme Regis and Charmouth","type":"experience","detail":"The beaches between the two towns give up ammonites and belemnites to anyone who looks, and this is where Mary Anning worked. Loose shingle, not the cliff face.","link":"https://www.peek.com/dorset-england-united-kingdom/r0knzx4/jurassic-coast-tour-fossil-hunting-adventure/a0k9waak","evidence":{"n_sources":7,"of":14,"urls":["https://www.visit-dorset.com/blog/post/top-10-things-to-do-on-the-jurassic-coast-in-dorset/","https://bristolhub.co.uk/jurassic-coast-2026-guide-best-fossils-beaches-and-views-in-dorset/","https://www.peek.com/dorset-england-united-kingdom/r0knzx4/jurassic-coast-tour-fossil-hunting-adventure/a0k9waak"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Walk the coast path","type":"trail","detail":"Ninety five miles from Exmouth to Old Harry Rocks, England's only natural World Heritage Site, and about six or seven days end to end. Golden Cap on the way is the highest point on the south coast.","season":[4,5,6,7,8,9,10],"evidence":{"n_sources":7,"of":14,"urls":["https://www.southwestcoastpath.org.uk/walk-coast-path/short-breaks/7-10-day-breaks/jurassic-coast/","https://www.dorsetwalks.co.uk/jurassic-coast-walk/","https://jurassiccoastpath.com/"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Old Harry Rocks","type":"activity","detail":"Chalk stacks marking the eastern end of the coast at Handfast Point. An easy walk of about 3.5 miles from Swanage to Studland goes past them.","evidence":{"n_sources":6,"of":14,"urls":["https://www.visitbritain.com/en/destinations/england/jurassic-coast","https://www.southwestcoastpath.org.uk/walk-coast-path/short-breaks/7-10-day-breaks/jurassic-coast/","https://www.swcp.org.uk/jurassic-coast-walks/"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Portland Bill and Chesil Beach","type":"activity","detail":"An eighteen mile shingle bank runs out to a limestone island. The five mile clifftop walk to the Bill passes old quarries and a sculpture park.","evidence":{"n_sources":5,"of":14,"urls":["https://www.southwestcoastpath.org.uk/walk-coast-path/short-breaks/7-10-day-breaks/jurassic-coast/","https://www.dorsetcouncil.gov.uk/sport-leisure/walking/walking-routes-and-trails/walking-in-weymouth-and-portland.aspx","https://www.heatheronhertravels.com/things-to-do-in-dorset/"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"The Cobb at Lyme Regis","type":"activity","detail":"The thirteenth century harbour wall the town grew behind, and a working breakwater still.","evidence":{"n_sources":4,"of":14,"urls":["https://www.southwestcoastpath.org.uk/walk-coast-path/short-breaks/7-10-day-breaks/jurassic-coast/","https://www.heatheronhertravels.com/things-to-do-in-dorset/","https://dorsettravelguide.com/dorset-jurassic-coast-highlights/"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]}],"nearby":{"beaches":[{"layer":"beaches","cc":"GB","id":"gb-monmouth-beach-Q6901052","name":"Monmouth Beach","km":3.6,"bearing":"NE","lat":50.7192,"lon":-2.943,"tier":1,"score":6.9,"thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Demolition_of_chalets_Monmouth_Beach_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3369983.jpg/500px-Demolition_of_chalets_Monmouth_Beach_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3369983.jpg","thumb_ok_print":true},{"layer":"beaches","cc":"GB","id":"gb-dawlish-warren-beach-relation19466330","name":"Dawlish Warren Beach","km":32.8,"bearing":"W","lat":50.60865,"lon":-3.4289,"tier